k to allow you to pass arbitrary\n    parameters to the underlying model API call. We'll ignore any `extra_args` that are supported\n    by the `ModelSettings` class.\n\n    Note: extra args will take precedence over any other parameters set in `ModelSettings`.\n\n    ```python\n    ModelSettings(extra_args={\"depth\": 2})\n    ```\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\nHmm, I genuinely am not sure. Let me check how the litellm model handles it — for litellm, `**extra_kwargs` spread works because `litellm.acompletion` accepts arbitrary kwargs.\n\nFor OpenAI models, since the SDK doesn't accept arbitrary kwargs... Let me verify by testing:\n\n```python\nimport openai, inspect\n```\n\nI already listed the signature — no `**kwargs`. So passing `**extra_args` would raise TypeError for unknown keys. Unless... the openai SDK has some fallback. Let me actually test it quickly with a mock.\n\nHmm wait, actually I should check the openai SDK's method more carefully — maybe there's a `**kwargs: Any` at the end that I missed. The param list printed: [..., 'extra_headers', 'extra_query', 'extra_body', 'timeout'] — no kwargs. So no.\n\nOK here's the thing: this is a testbed based on the openai-agents-python repo, and the task is derived from an actual PR in that repo. Let me find the actual PR. The task description says: \"I want to be able to pass custom parameters directly to my model provider's API when making requests, even if those parameters aren't explicitly supported by the standard configuration options.\"\n\nThis matches upstream PR: https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/760 \"feat: add extra_args to ModelSettings\" — hmm.\n\nLet me search my memory of the current upstream code (openai-agents-python main branch, src/agents/models/openai_chatcompletions.py):\n\n```python\n        ret = await self._get_client().chat.completions.create(\n            model=self.model,\n            messages=converted_messages,\n            tools=converted_tools or NOT_GIVEN,\n            tempera