{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788504700-AZNWBR14fyFd38UbjCs5","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, there's a subtlety: the spread `**extra_args` could collide with a named kwarg like `metadata` or `temperature` if the user passes e.g. `extra_args={\"temperature\": 0.9}`. Python would raise `TypeError: create() got multiple values for keyword argument 'temperature'`. That's the upstream behavior too (later upstream added an explicit nice error for this). The upstream commit at this point just did `**(model_settings.extra_args or {})` which has the same collision behavior. So this matches upstream semantics — the error message is even informative (\"got multiple values for keyword argument\"). Fine.\n\nNow the litellm model.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2c365a3-3bdc-4731-a977-75aced7bea21","uuid":"52215da4-c67d-4350-ad12-534cd03bea52","timestamp":"2026-09-04T06:51:42.732Z","request_id":"gen-1788504700-AZNWBR14fyFd38UbjCs5"}
