{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788504769-4ISFVp4itBqTM1HYrr6g","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a great template — `tests/test_extra_headers.py` covers both Responses and ChatCompletions with dummy clients. I'll write `tests/models/test_kwargs_functionality.py` following the upstream tests (litellm + chatcompletions) and add a responses test plus None-filtering tests.\n\nNote: the DummyResponses mock for the responses model in test_extra_headers.py returns an object with `output=[]`, `usage`, `id`. That works with `get_response` which does `response.output`, `response.usage`, `response.id`. Note `_debug.DONT_LOG_MODEL_DATA` — logger.debug with json.dumps of `[x.model_dump() for x in response.output]` — empty list so fine.\n\nFor the chatcompletions model, the mock needs `base_url` since `get_response` builds `model_config=... | {\"base_url\": str(self._client.base_url)}`.\n\nFor litellm test — upstream uses monkeypatch on `litellm.acompletion`. Note that `LitellmModel.get_response` asserts `isinstance(response.choices[0], litellm.types.utils.Choices)` and converts message; the upstream fake returns `ModelResponse(choices=[choice], usage=Usage(0, 0, 0))` where msg = Message(role=\"assistant\", content=\"test response\"). Good.\n\nNote: `Usage(0, 0, 0)` — litellm's Usage signature is Usage(prompt_tokens, completion_tokens, total_tokens...). OK per upstream.\n\nOne concern: `Converter.message_to_output_items` on the converted ChatCompletionMessage — works upstream.\n\nNow write the test file. I'll mirror upstream's three tests exactly, then add:\n- `test_openai_responses_kwargs_forwarded`\n- `test_none_values_are_filtered` for litellm and chatcompletions/responses\n\nLet me now write the file.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_inp