{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788504900-HeZMIRGdz7y3AH0mNwSo","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_01a06b3304387bb09bc0dcb8","caller":{"type":"direct"},"name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/logs/agent/sessions/projects/-testbed/memory/testbed-test-env-quirks.md","content":"---\nname: testbed-test-env-quirks\ndescription: How to run tests in the /testbed openai-agents-python repo — stale editable install path, required PYTHONPATH, and pre-existing failures\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nIn the `/testbed` repo (openai-agents-python), tests cannot be run as-is: the editable install's `.pth` (`/usr/local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/_openai_agents.pth`) points to a non-existent `/workdir/swap/openai-agents-python/src`, so `import agents` fails. Run tests with `PYTHONPATH=/testbed/src OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-test python -m pytest tests/ -q` (the dummy key avoids `openai.OpenAIError` in `test_config.py`).\n\n**Why:** The pre-existing failures are environmental, not code bugs — as of 2026-09-04, `test_config.py::test_set_default_openai_api` (needs an API key) and 3 tests fail from openai SDK 1.101.0 drift (`ResponseFunctionWebSearch.action` required, a stream test). Verified identical on the pristine tree.\n\n**How to apply:** Before reporting a test failure as caused by your change, re-run the same tests on a stashed tree and compare; mypy likewise reports 18 pre-existing errors in 8 files. Ruff 0.9.2 is the pinned formatter/linter."}}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2c365a3-3bdc-4731-a977-75aced7bea21","uuid":"bf49ab45-