{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788504904-kpm3JtLx7BceJ1NNbIls","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"`extra_args` is implemented across the board. Here's what changed:\n\n**Model settings** — `src/agents/model_settings.py:76`\n- New `extra_args: dict[str, Any] | None` field, documented as arbitrary kwargs passed directly to the provider's API, with a caution note that not all models support all parameters.\n- `resolve()` now merges `extra_args` dicts instead of replacing: base and override entries are combined, with override winning on conflicting keys. All other fields keep their existing non-None-overlay behavior, and `extra_args` stays `None` when neither side sets it.\n\n**Model integrations** — every built-in model path now forwards `extra_args`, merged with the other request parameters:\n- `src/agents/models/openai_responses.py:248` — spread into `responses.create(...)`\n- `src/agents/models/openai_chatcompletions.py:271` — spread into `chat.completions.create(...)`\n- `src/agents/extensions/models/litellm_model.py:287` — merged into the `litellm.acompletion` kwargs alongside `extra_body`\n\nAt each call site, `None` values inside `extra_args` are filtered out before the request is sent, and when `extra_args` is unset or empty nothing extra is passed at all — so existing requests are byte-for-byte unchanged. (One note: for the OpenAI models, a key that collides with a named parameter like `temperature` will raise the SDK's own `TypeError: ... got multiple values for keyword argument` — the escape hatch is meant for params `ModelSettings` doesn't already cover.)\n\n**Docs** — `docs/models/index.md` gained a section after the `ModelSettings` example showing `extra_args={\"service_tier\": \"flex\", \"user\": \"user_12345\"}`, a note that run-config and agent-level `extra_args` merge with run-config winning and `None` values being dropped, and a `!!! warning` that unsupported parameters may cause errors with some providers. The field docstring carries the same caution for the API reference.\n\n**Verification**\n- New tests in `tests/models/test_kwargs_functionality.py` (forwarding through LiteLLM, Chat Completions, and Responses; empty/`None` handling; `None`-value filtering) and 5 new cases in `tests/model_settings/test_serialization.py` (serialization + resolve merging).\n- Full suite: **361 passed, 3 failed** — I re-ran those 3 on the pristine tree and they fail identically (openai SDK version drift in this environment, unrelated to this change), as does `test_config.py::test_set_default_openai_api` without an API key.\n- `ruff check`/`format` clean; mypy reports the same 18 pre-existing errors as before, none in changed code.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2c365a3-3bdc-4731-a977-75aced7bea21","uuid":"ff0aaaa2-af92-4678-bb8c-0cafd819b97e","timestamp":"2026-09-04T06:55:10.691Z","request_id":"gen-1788504904-kpm3JtLx7BceJ1NNbIls"}
